    54	
    55	### 1.1 Exact completion along the intrinsic divisor `Phi`
    56	
    57	Let `P=(A,U)` and `q=U^2-A-A^2Z`.  Complete the ambient polynomial ring at
    58	`(A,U)`.  Since `R/P=C[Z]` and `q_A=-1-2AZ` is a unit in that completion, the
    59	formal implicit-function theorem gives a unique zero-constant-term solution
    60	`A=a(u,Z)` of
    61	
    62	```text
    63	A+ZA^2=U^2
    64	```
    65	
    66	With `u=U`, it is
    67	
    68	```text
    69	a(u,Z)=U^2-ZU^4+2Z^2U^6-5Z^3U^8+...
    70	      =(sqrt(1+4ZU^2)-1)/(2Z),
    71	```
    72	
    73	where the quotient denotes its power series and is valid also at `Z=0`.
    74	This gives an isomorphism directly; only after it is obtained does the
    75	extended ideal become `(a(u,Z),u)=(u)`, since `a(u,Z) in (u^2)`.  Therefore
    76	
    77	```text
    78	R^_P  = C[Z][[u]],             R^_(R_P)=C(Z)[[u]],       (1.1)
    79	A |-> a(u,Z),                  U |-> u.
    80	```
    81	
    82	Here the first expression is the formal completion along the whole affine
    83	line and the second is the complete DVR at its generic point.  At the closed
    84	point `p_z0=(A,U,Z-z0)`, one similarly has
    85	
    86	```text
    87	O^_(S,p_z0)=C[[u,w]],          w=Z-z0.                  (1.2)
