   118	If
   119	
   120	```text
   121	F=h(Z)u^m+O(u^(m+1)),       G=k(Z)u^n+O(u^(n+1)),
   122	```
   123	
   124	then
   125	
   126	```text
   127	nu({F,G}) >= m+n-1,                                      (1.4)
   128	in_(m+n-1){F,G}
   129	 =2(m h k'-n h' k)u^(m+n-1).                            (1.5)
   130	```
   131	
   132	Here and in (1.9), a prime means differentiation with respect to the residue
   133	coordinate `Z`; it is not a branch or prime-divisor label.
   134	
   135	Equation (1.4) is only a floor: (1.5) can vanish.  For fixed `H` it gives
   136	
   137	```text
   138	nu(X_H^j F) >= nu(F)+j(nu(H)-1),                         (1.6)
   139	```
   140	
   141	again with equality only while the successive initial expressions do not
   142	cancel.  This is the exact associated-graded Hamiltonian structure, rather
   143	than a scalar-weight proxy for membership in `R`.
