   310	The map `g:C_f->A1` is surjective etale of degree four.  Let
   311	`Cbar_f` be its smooth projective completion, of genus `gamma_f`, and write
   312	
   313	```text
   314	Sigma=Cbar_f-C_f=Sigma_infty disjoint_union Sigma_fin,
   315	r_infty=#Sigma_infty,          s_fin=#Sigma_fin.
   316	```
   317	
   318	For `p in Sigma`, let `e_p` be the ramification index of the completed map
   319	`gbar:Cbar_f->P1`.  The following divisor is an exact invariant of the
   320	completed Hamiltonian flow:
   321	
   322	```text
   323	div_Cbar_f(D)
   324	 =sum_(p in Sigma_infty)(e_p+1)p
   325	  -sum_(p in Sigma_fin)(e_p-1)p.                        (2.1)
   326	```
   327	
   328	Indeed, at a finite deleted point one can choose a uniformizer `z` with
   329	`g-g(p)=z^e`.  At a point over infinity choose it with `g=z^(-e)`.  Since
   330	`D(g)=kappa`, respectively
   331	
   332	```text
   333	D=(kappa/e)z^(1-e)partial_z,                            (2.2)
   334	D=-(kappa/e)z^(e+1)partial_z.                           (2.3)
   335	```
   336	
   337	There are no zeros or poles on `C_f`, because `g` is etale there.  This proves
   338	(2.1), including attainment at every place.  It also gives exact iterate
   339	growth:
   340	
   341	```text
   342	finite p:
   343	 D^j(z)=(kappa/e)^j product_(i=1)^(j-1)(1-ie)
   344	          z^(1-je),
   345	
   346	infinity p:
   347	 D^j(z)=(-kappa/e)^j product_(i=1)^(j-1)(1+ie)
   348	          z^(1+je).                                    (2.4)
   349	```
   350	
   351	At a finite ramified point `e>=2`, the first coefficient product never
   352	vanishes, so the pole order of `D^j(z)` is exactly `je-1`.
   353	
   354	Taking degrees in (2.1), or equivalently applying Riemann--Hurwitz, gives
   355	
   356	```text
   357	deg Zero(D)=sum_infinity(e_p+1)=4+r_infty,
   358	deg Pole(D)=sum_fin(e_p-1)=2gamma_f+2+r_infty,
