   362	In particular the finite ramification sum is positive.  This turns the local
   363	formula into another global non-local-finiteness witness.  Choose a finite
   364	ramified `p`, and by Riemann--Roch choose `h in O(C_f)` with its only pole at
   365	`p`, of order `M>0`.  Then
   366	
   367	```text
   368	ord_p(D^j h)=-M-je                                     (2.6)
   369	```
   370	
   371	for all `j`; these iterates are linearly independent.  Since
   372	`O(C_f)=R/(f-a_f)` and `(f-a_f)` is `X_f`-stable, local finiteness on `R` would
   373	descend to the quotient.  Thus (2.6) proves `X_f` non-locally-finite from the
   374	degree-four fibre structure itself.  Interchanging `f` and `g` proves the
   375	same statement for `X_g`.
