   235	relative algebraic closure of `C(g)` in `K`.  If its degree were greater than
   236	one, Riemann--Hurwitz for its projective Stein curve would again force a
   237	ramified point over a finite `g`-value.  Factoring `Y` through
   238	`T_g x A1_f` would then produce a ramified divisor of `Y-S` mapping onto the
   239	horizontal line `{g=a}`.  The frozen census does not expressly exclude it,
   240	so the analogous proposed route stops at
   241	
   242	```text
   243	OPEN[census-exhaustivity-g]: no horizontal irreducible component occurs
   244	in the codimension-one ramified boundary image of Y->A2.
   245	```
   246	
   247	The intrinsic proof is fully symmetric.  The projective curve of `L_g` is
   248	`P1`; its affine normalization embeds in `R`; and `R^*=C^*` forces it to have
   249	one point at infinity.  Thus its ring is `C[t]` and `g=Q(t)`.  Now
   250	
   251	```text
   252	kappa={f,g}=Q'(t){f,t}.
   253	```
   254	
   255	It follows that `Q'(t)` is a unit of `R`, hence a nonzero constant, so
   256	`deg Q=1`.  Therefore
   257	
   258	```text
   259	C(g) is algebraically closed in K,
   260	```
   261	
   262	and the general `g`-fibre is geometrically irreducible and connected.
   263	
   264	Nothing in the intrinsic argument breaks under the interchange.  Only the
   265	unused boundary route changes direction: it would need `B` nonvertical for
   266	`f` and nonhorizontal for `g`, both of which follow from the cusp, as well as
   267	the missing exhaustivity clauses.  The exceptional-value discussion is
   268	likewise symmetric, with horizontal tangencies and the `g`-coordinates of
   269	the listed special sets substituted for their vertical counterparts.
   270	
   271	## 5. Repaired identities and partition table
   272	
   273	Fix `h in {f,g}`, let `k` denote the other coordinate, and choose a general
   274	value as in §§3.4--4.  Let `Cbar_h` be the smooth connected projective
   275	completion of `C_h`, let `gamma_h` be its genus, and split the deleted places
   276	as `Sigma_infty` over `k=infinity` and `Sigma_fin` over finite `k`.  Put
   277	`r_h=#Sigma_infty`, and let `e_p` be the local degree of the completed mate
   278	map `kbar:Cbar_h->P1`.  Its total degree is four.
   279	
   280	### 5.1 Repaired (2.5)
   281	
   282	The exact local vector-field divisor from (2.1) and Riemann--Hurwitz give
   283	
   284	```text
   285	deg Zero(X_h|C_h)=sum_(p in Sigma_infty)(e_p+1)=4+r_h,
   286	deg Pole(X_h|C_h)=sum_(p in Sigma_fin)(e_p-1)
   287	                  =2gamma_h+2+r_h,
   288	deg div(X_h|C_h)=2-2gamma_h.                 (2.5-repaired)
   289	```
   290	
   291	This is now justified because `Cbar_h` is one connected curve.  Indeed,
   292	`sum_infty e_p=4`, while Riemann--Hurwitz says
   293	
   294	```text
   295	2gamma_h-2=-8+sum_all(e_p-1).
   296	```
   297	
   298	### 5.2 Repaired (3.2) and the four rows
   299	
   300	For the additional generality conditions in §§3.4--4, every finite deleted
   301	place is transverse of index two, and their number is
   302	
   303	```text
   304	d_h=deg(h o beta_B).
   305	```
   306	
   307	Therefore the finite ramification sum in (2.5-repaired) is `d_h`, so
   308	
   309	```text
   310	d_h=2gamma_h+2+r_h.                         (3.2-repaired)
   311	```
   312	
   313	The pole orders of `k` over infinity form a positive partition `lambda_h` of
   314	four, of length `r_h`.  The complete necessary table is consequently
   315	
   316	| `r_h` | `lambda_h` | necessary `d_h` |
   317	|---:|---|---:|
   318	| 1 | `(4)` | `2gamma_h+3` |
   319	| 2 | `(3,1)` or `(2,2)` | `2gamma_h+4` |
   320	| 3 | `(2,1,1)` | `2gamma_h+5` |
   321	| 4 | `(1,1,1,1)` | `2gamma_h+6` |
   322	
   323	These rows are necessary, not sufficient, and assert no attainment of a
   324	tuple.  They apply separately to `f` and `g`; the charged data give no
   325	equality between the two genera or between the two infinity partitions.
   326	
   327	### 5.3 Repaired closure (3.6)
   328	
   329	A supplied pair of tuples `(d_h,gamma_h,r_h,lambda_h)` is excluded if any of
   330	the following holds:
   331	
   332	```text
   333	d_f<=2 or d_g<=2;
   334	d_h-r_h-2 notin 2Z_(>=0) for some h in {f,g};
   335	gamma_h != (d_h-r_h-2)/2 for some h in {f,g};
   336	lambda_h is not a positive partition of 4 of length r_h
   337	    for some h in {f,g}.                       (3.6-repaired)
   338	```
   339	
   340	The third line is the missing consistency clause.  Equivalently, do not
   341	supply `gamma_h` independently, but define it by
   342	
   343	```text
   344	gamma_h=(d_h-r_h-2)/2.
   345	```
   346	
   347	Without this clause, for example, `(d,r,gamma,lambda)=(5,1,17,(4))` passes
   348	the three literal old tests despite contradicting (3.2-repaired).
   349	
   350	### 5.4 Correct provenance of (2.6)
   351	
   352	Once a finite deleted ramified place `p` of index `e_p` is known, the
   353	Riemann--Roch witness and local calculation are valid.  If `H` has its only
   354	pole on `Cbar_h` at `p`, of order `M>0`, then
   355	
   356	```text
   357	ord_p((X_h|C_h)^j H)=-M-j e_p,                         (2.6)
   358	lc_p((X_h|C_h)^j H)
   359	 =(kappa/e_p)^j lc_p(H)
   360	   product_(i=0)^(j-1)(-M-i e_p) != 0,
   361	```
   362	
   363	up to the harmless sign change coming from whether `h=f` or `g`.  Thus the
   364	orders are attained and the iterates are linearly independent.
   365	
   366	The existence of `p` did not follow from the phrase “total degree four”
   367	alone: a disconnected fully split degree-four control can have no finite
   368	ramification.  There are two valid provenance routes in the repaired packet.
   369	First, the connectedness theorem above plus (2.5-repaired) makes the finite
   370	ramification sum `2gamma_h+2+r_h>0`.  Second, independently, a general
   371	transverse intersection with the noncoordinate boundary `B` supplies an
   372	index-two place (because `d_h>0`).  Formula (2.6) itself is local once either
   373	route has supplied that place.
   374	
   375	## 6. Other surviving corrections
   376	
   377	At the interior companion over the target cusp, put
   378	
   379	```text
   380	p=f-f(u_c),                    q=g-g(u_c).
   381	```
   382	
   383	Etaleness gives the exact marked completion and fields
   384	
   385	```text
   386	Ohat_(S,u_c)=C[[p,q]],
   387	X_f=kappa partial_q,           X_g=-kappa partial_p.       (1.11)
   388	```
   389	
   390	The safe cusp-companion conclusion is narrower than “no local invariant can
   391	detect wildness”:
   392	
   393	> The unmarked formal conjugacy class of the vector-field germ, and hence any
   394	> fixed finite jet of that unmarked germ, cannot detect global
   395	> non-local-finiteness.  Full marked expansions of distinguished global
   396	> algebra generators can detect it.
   397	
   398	Indeed, the unmarked pair is the same translation pair as on the tame affine
   399	plane.  Once the embedding of `R` and the labels `A,U,Z` are retained,
   400	however, local finiteness is equivalent to a constant-coefficient polynomial
   401	recurrence for every generator orbit.  Global non-local-finiteness therefore
   402	forces at least one full marked generator series to fail such a recurrence.
   403	This is infinite-jet data; the polynomial cusp equation itself and any fixed
   404	finite jet remain unable to witness it.
   405	
   406	With the connectedness repair, the packet's local divisor formula (2.1),
   407	uniformizer iterate formula (2.4), and the conditional local calculation
   408	(2.6) survive exactly.  The generic transverse-boundary calculation and its
   409	independent non-local-finiteness witness also survive.  Nothing here supplies
   410	the special length-three cusp-boundary completion, a cusp Puiseux expansion,
   411	or an existence theorem for any row of the necessary table.
   412	
   413	## 7. Conclusions and typed open points
   414	
   415	The hidden premise is now discharged: for `h=f` and `h=g`,
   416	
   417	```text
   418	C(h)^alg intersect K=C(h),
   419	```
   420	
   421	where the algebraic closure is taken inside `K`.  Thus the general coordinate
   422	fibres are geometrically irreducible, and (2.5), (3.2), the four-row table,
   423	and (3.6) are valid in the repaired connected forms of §5.  In particular a
   424	recorded genus must obey `gamma_h=(d_h-r_h-2)/2`.
   425	
   426	Two limitations remain, neither affecting that verdict:
   427	
   428	1. `OPEN[CENSUS-EXHAUSTIVITY]`: the frozen inputs do not say that `B` is the
   429	   entire codimension-one boundary or branch image.  Consequently the
   430	   pre-review's proposed *boundary* proof stops at this interface.  The
